# Production HA deploy

Cloud production runs dual gateway via `docker-compose.prod.ha.yml`
(`gateway-a` + `gateway-b` + Postgres + Redis on `card-rules-assistant_default`).
Public path: Caddy `/gw` → both instances.

## Daily release

```bash
cd ~/workspace/llm-gateway
./scripts/rollout_ha.sh
```

Rebuilds one instance at a time and waits for healthy so the other keeps serving.

## Do not

- `docker compose -f docker-compose.prod.ha.yml up -d --build` on **both** gateways together (causes downtime)
- `docker compose down -v` (destroys Postgres/Redis volumes)
- Point Caddy back at the old single `gateway:8000` service

## First-time / cutover only

Initial bring-up and Caddy dual-upstream cutover are documented in `deploy/README.md` (HA section). After cutover, use `rollout_ha.sh` only.
